{
  "id": "contract-rewrite-001",
  "schema": "subagent-report-v1",
  "profile": "coder",
  "findings": [
    {
      "id": "finding-001",
      "text": "Core Conclusion: The statement 'docker compose always restarts failed containers, so our backend is self-healing' conflates a default behavior with a guarantee. Docker Compose restarts containers whose main process exits, but this is not unconditional, and 'self-healing' is an overstatement without additional health-check and restart-policy configuration.",
      "layer": "L1"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-002",
      "text": "Epistemic Breakdown: [L1 - Axiom] Docker Compose, by default, restarts containers when their main process exits, based on the restart policy (e.g., 'unless-stopped' or 'always') specified in the compose file or defaulting to 'no' in some versions.",
      "layer": "L1"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-003",
      "text": "Epistemic Breakdown: [L2 - Observed Evidence] In our environment, we have observed that when the backend container process crashes, it is automatically restarted by the Docker daemon. This is a specific observed behavior, not a general truth.",
      "layer": "L2"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-004",
      "text": "Epistemic Breakdown: [L3 - Heuristic] The heuristic is: 'if the main process exits, restart it, and thus the backend is self-healing.' This is a reasonable operational assumption for simple crash recovery, but it is not a full self-healing solution.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-005",
      "text": "Confidence Ceiling: The conclusion 'our backend is self-healing' has a confidence ceiling of L2 (observed evidence), because the general claim 'docker compose always restarts' is an axiom that is not universally true (e.g., if restart policy is set to 'no', or if the container is stopped manually). Therefore, the confidence cannot exceed the weakest layer supporting it, which is L2 at best.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-006",
      "text": "Evidence Gaps: (1) The exact restart policy in the compose file is not specified; if it is not 'always' or 'unless-stopped', the claim is false. (2) The observed behavior is not quantified (how many times, under what failure modes). (3) 'Self-healing' is not defined; does it include recovering from deadlocks, OOM kills, or health check failures? (4) No health check is mentioned; Docker Compose restarts on exit, not on unhealthy status.",
      "layer": "L3"
    },
    {
      "id": "finding-007",
      "text": "Scope and Counterexamples for [L3]: The heuristic applies only to main-process exit. It does NOT apply when: (1) the container is stopped by a user or orchestrator; (2) the container is killed by OOM killer unless restart policy is set; (3) the process hangs and does not exit; (4) the host is down; (5) the restart limit is reached (due to backoff).",
      "layer": "L3"
    }
  ],
  "evidence": [
    {
      "id": "evidence-001",
      "kind": "knowledge",
      "description": "Docker Compose restart policies: 'no', 'always', 'on-failure', 'unless-stopped'. Default is 'no' in many Compose versions; 'always' is not the default."
    },
    {
      "id": "evidence-002",
      "kind": "observation",
      "description": "User-stated observation: 'docker compose always restarts failed containers' — assumed to be an observed behavior in their environment, but not a universal fact."
    }
  ],
  "confidence_cap": "L2",
  "gaps": [
    "Restart policy in the compose file is not confirmed.",
    "The definition of 'failed container' and 'self-healing' is ambiguous.",
    "No evidence of health check integration; restart on exit is not equivalent to self-healing.",
    "No counterexample testing: what happens when the host reboots? When the process hangs? When OOM-killed?"
  ],
  "recommendation": "Rewrite the claim as: 'We observed that Docker Compose restarts our backend container when its main process exits (restart policy: always), which handles crash recovery. However, this is not full self-healing; we need to add health checks and define recovery procedures for hanging processes, OOM kills, and dependency failures. To validate, we should set restart: always in the compose file, add a healthcheck command, and monitor restart counts; if the backend does not restart within 5 seconds after a kill, the assumption fails.'"
}

